--- body ---
## Context
Measured 2026-11-01 on padme with sentinel probes (rules/README.md § Loading per
runtime): Claude Code loads the four resident rules in every session (TUI and
`-p`); Codex (`exec`) and Pi (`--print`) load none of them, guards.md
included. Both load the project's AGENTS.md and the session-start hook output.
rules/README.md already says the adapters "must inject" the resident set; none
does.

Only Claude Code has a rules/ concept (`~/.claude/rules`, `paths:` for
conditional loading, HTML comments stripped). Codex reads AGENTS.md from
`$CODEX_HOME` then the project hierarchy (capped by `project_doc_max_bytes`);
its `~/.codex/rules/*.rules` are command policies, not instructions. Pi reads
context files from `~/.pi/agent/`, the cwd and its parents, and extensions can
add instructions. Neither strips HTML comments.

## Approach
Generate, never hand-maintain: at install time an adapter writes one global
file from the four resident rules minus claude-code.md, HTML comments stripped
(Codex: `~/.codex/AGENTS.md`; Pi: `~/.pi/agent/AGENTS.md` or the idh-guard
extension). Conditional rules stay reachable through the skills that name them.
Writing a global file changes every session of that runtime on the host: the
install step is the author's to run or approve.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] The sentinel probe finds workflow.md, git.md and guards.md text in Codex and Pi sessions, and no HTML comment text
- [ ] The generated files are rebuilt by the installer when rules/ changes (no hand-edited copy)
- [ ] rules/README.md § Loading per runtime updated from a new measurement

## Imagine (raid 1f0534)
- Premise holds: rules/README.md says adapters must inject the resident set; none does.
- Simplest path: one generator script (resident rules minus claude-code.md, HTML comments stripped) called by the installer; tests on the generator output. Writing `~/.codex/AGENTS.md` / `~/.pi/agent/AGENTS.md` on the host is the author's to run (ticket says so): the PR ships the generator and installer step, the install and the sentinel re-probe wait for the author, so this PR refs 1413 and does not close it.
- Runs after 1416 (shared installer) and 1412 (guards.md content).

